{
 "description": "Real-worm imitation as a start for C.2's fit (description; band cohorts; discarded seeds).\n\nC.2 learns its first actions from real worms rather than from C.1, so its start owes nothing to the\nmechanistic model. Scheer & Bargmann 2023's wild-type band-cohort animals (PD1074, od2) on the small\nlawn and in the uniform well are replayed through the simulator:\n\n- **The frame.** Each second's position is placed in the assay's arena. On the small lawn the radius\n  is normalised by the lawn edge at the worm's angle, so the real edge lands on the simulated lawn's\n  rim; in the uniform well the position is scaled into the well (4.9 mm over the farthest real\n  point). The heading is the motion's direction, turned by pi in a reversal and held below 0.02 mm.\n- **The senses.** The evaluator's own sensing, eating and satiety along the path, satiety started\n  where the assay's analysis window opens (1,200 s). A shadow C.2 advances its modulators on those\n  senses and its own settled activity; each second's state is stored with the real action.\n- **The targets.** On a run second (no reversal or omega flag in it or the second before): the run\n  speed's and the curvature's raw values (2v/v_max - 1, and the heading change over omega_max, the\n  curvature only where this and the previous displacement are at least 0.03 mm), scored by the\n  Gaussian density of their atanh under the network's mean and log-SD. On every second after a run\n  second: a reversal onset, an omega onset or neither (a delta turn is not flagged, so it falls in\n  neither); a bout is a run of its per-frame flag after one-frame gaps are merged, kept if it lasts\n  at least two frames, the kinematics check's rule (`primitive_kinematics_check.bouts`), scored by the primitives' start probabilities with the hazard outputs' noise integrated\n  over 16 draws. Seconds with a missing frame, and the first 120 s, are left out.\n- **Training.** Adam (lr 0.01, batches of 4,096, the two assays weighted equally) on the encoder's\n  learnable tensors from the box centre jittered by 0.01 (the speed noise's timescale at 1 s, as\n  the curriculum pilot sets it, and held), three rounds of 10 epochs, the shadow\n  re-rolled before each round with the trained network, the vector projected onto the box every 20\n  steps. 20% of animals are held out to score the fit (speed R^2, reversal-onset AUC), beside the\n  boosting probe's ceiling from geometric senses (`realworm_predictability.json`: speed R^2 0.64,\n  AUC 0.59).\n- **Closed loop.** The answer is graded on 200 animals (every family and the three mutants) on\n  851,000,000 + i, on 4 workers beside the curriculum pilot.\n\nRun from the repository root: `realworm_imitation.py [smoke]`.\n",
